Subject: [PATCH] http: keep Firefox as the name in the User-Agent

The engine builds its User-Agent from the application's name unless the
project file gives it another one. With --with-app-basename=Nulavio every
request, and navigator.userAgent, ended in "Nulavio/159.0.1" instead of
"Firefox/159.0". That names a small group of people to every site they visit,
gives away the point release, and is a value that sites looking for Firefox do
not recognise. With this the User-Agent is the one Firefox itself sends on
the same system. Like the vendor (patch 0001), the option can only be implied
by the project configure file.

Nothing else reads the option: about:support, the profile location, the
window class and the add-on application ID are unchanged.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not applicable (Firefox's own build has this name already; Fenix
sets the same option in mobile/android/moz.configure).
---
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@
 
 
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_VENDOR", "Nulavio")
+# Nulavio: the User-Agent keeps saying Firefox. Without this the engine uses
+# the application's own name, and every request and navigator.userAgent would
+# carry "Nulavio/<version>": a label for a small group of people, and a value
+# sites that look for Firefox do not recognise.
+imply_option("MOZ_APP_UA_NAME", "Firefox")
 imply_option("MOZ_APP_ID", "{ec8030f7-c20a-464f-9b0e-13a3a9e97384}")
 # Include the DevTools client, not just the server (which is the default)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEVTOOLS", "all")
